  "id": "normative-influence",
  "term": "normative influence",
  "definition": "Normative influence is the effect of social norms on a person’s judgments or choices, especially when they look to other people for guidance. In uncertain situations, this influence can become stronger because following others may also help reduce feelings such as anxiety or frustration.",
